Matthew reports that the foreigners “opened their treasures ” and presented Jesus with gold, frankincense, and myrrh.
Interestingly, those expensive gifts may have come at just the right time, since Jesus ’ family ​ — evidently of little means — ​ were soon forced to flee as refugees. ​ — Matthew 2: 11 - 15.
While Jesus ’ conception was miraculous, the rest of Mary’s children were conceived naturally with her husband, Joseph. ​ — Matthew 1: 25.
